  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), seen from the pilot side above-left: throttle (attached) on the left with its right face and thumb buttons toward the camera, stick head buttons facing the camera, base buttons between them",
  "mappingSource": "catalog (thrustmaster.json): button numbers per EDRefCard bindingsData/DeviceMappings (https://github.com/richardbuckle/EDRefCard) and https://github.com/machinedgod/tflight4: 1 trigger (R1), 2 L1, 3 R3, 4 L3, 5-8 square/cross/circle/triangle, 9 R2, 10 L2, 11 SHARE, 12 OPTIONS; axes per the Thrustmaster control panel picture https://ts.thrustmaster.com/download/pictures/PCMAC/TFH4/CPL_TFH4_Fw25.png (Slider0 rocker, RZ twist, Z throttle, X/Y handle). Thrustmaster's own TFH4 manual (https://ts.thrustmaster.com/download/accessories/Manuals/TFH4/T-Flight_Hotas_4_Manual.pdf) names no button numbers; positions read from the PlayStation labels printed on the device",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "note": "No vendor number map for the TFH4. The T.Flight Hotas One (same body) prints \"2\" under the centre key and \"4\" under the right flank key, which supports the catalog (L1 = 2, L3 = 4). The T.Flight Hotas X PC preset diagram (https://ts.thrustmaster.com/download/accessories/Manuals/TFHX/t-flight_hotas_X_manual.pdf p.5) instead seems to point 3 at the right flank; the reviewer may verify L3/R3 on a real device. The trigger (R1), R2/L2 and the rudder rocker sit on the faces turned away from the camera.",
